\f1\b\fs28 \cf0 \strokec2 D. Branch-kind invariants\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 D1. RootBranch invariant.
\f0\b0 \uc0\u8232 A root branch has no parents and contributes only its own local branch positions.\

\f1\b D2. TreeBranch invariant.
\f0\b0 \uc0\u8232 A tree branch has exactly one parent anchor position. Upward historical inclusion from a position on this branch continues through that single parent.\

\f1\b D3. DagBranch invariant.
\f0\b0 \uc0\u8232 A DAG branch has exactly two parent anchor positions. Upward historical inclusion from a position on this branch includes both parent histories, and comparisons must account for both.\
This is the semantic foundation for merges.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
